@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nhi-il25-nouns`
IMPORT `nhi-il25-published-figures`
IMPORT `nhi-s14-income`
IMPORT `nhi-s14-fixed-and-benefits`
IMPORT `nhi-s14-month`

-- INDEPENDENT TESTS for row IL-25 (BACKLOG IL-56), written by fid-il-25 from DECIDED-ANSWERS.md,
-- which was frozen (sha256 ca4fee908677c7fd0720382e967d8ce9dd1482180d060c54a64176fcad1434a5)
-- before this encoding was opened. Case ids C01 to C80 are those of DECIDED-ANSWERS.md.
-- Expected values are the tester's, to four decimals, and none was changed to match the encoding.
--
-- Readings used (the tester's decided reading of each fork; the encoding's default declines):
--   F1 the maximum caps the income (A1);  F2 the income is what is paid (no minimum income is passed);
--   F3 the reduced rate applies to a benefit and an early pension (A3);
--   F4 section 14(e) displaces (b) to (d) for a pensioner (A4);  F6 one reduced amount across (no case turns on it).
--
-- EXPECTED REFUSALS (declared in check.sh, one line per assertion; class SCOPE: the encoding answers
-- only contribution months from January 2026): C66, C67, C68, C69, C70, C71, C73 assert the tester's
-- 2025 and 2024 values and the encoding refuses them; C40, C72, C74 and C75 assert REFUSED and are satisfied.

§ `Independent tests`

`kind: employee` MEANS `an employee for whom the employer is liable for National Insurance contributions`
`kind: employee himself` MEANS `an employee who is liable for National Insurance contributions himself because the employer is not`
`kind: self-employed` MEANS `a self-employed person who is liable for National Insurance contributions himself`
`kind: neither` MEANS `an insured person who is neither an employee nor a self-employed person liable for National Insurance contributions himself`
`kind: early pension` MEANS `one who is paid an early pension, a retirement grant or an adjustment allowance`
`kind: nothing payable` MEANS `an insured person for whom nothing is payable under section 14(b) to (e1) or (f1)`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, hw IS A BOOLEAN, st IS A BOOLEAN, s7 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The facts that decide the exemptions of section 14(g) and (g1)`
`flags` a hw st s7 MEANS
    `The facts that decide the exemptions of section 14(g) and (g1)` WITH
        `age in whole years at the start of the month` IS a
        `a housewife within section 238 of the National Insurance Law` IS hw
        `a student or recruit exempt under section 351(11)(2a) or (2b) of the National Insurance Law` IS st
        `exempt under section 351(7a) or (11)(2c) of the National Insurance Law` IS s7
        `a living organ donor in a month the Minister of Health has set for the donor` IS FALSE

`no flags` MEANS `flags` 35 FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER
      k IS A `A kind of insured person under section 14`
      x IS A NUMBER, ex IS A NUMBER
      pc IS A `What old-age pension an insured person is paid`
      sp IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A `The facts that decide the exemptions of section 14(g) and (g1)`
GIVETH A `A person's month under section 14`
`mo` y m k x ex pc sp e MEANS
    `A person's month under section 14` WITH
        `year` IS y
        `month` IS m
        `kind` IS k
        `income` IS x
        `income exempt under section 350A(a) of the National Insurance Law` IS ex
        `minimum income for the person under Schedule K` IS NOTHING
        `old-age pension` IS pc
        `the pension is raised by a spouse's supplement or a spouse's pension` IS sp
        `exemptions` IS e

GIVEN k IS A `A kind of insured person under section 14`, x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A person's month under section 14`
`p` k x MEANS `mo` 2026 3 k x 0 `no old-age pension` FALSE `no flags`

GIVEN k IS A `A kind of insured person under section 14`, x IS A NUMBER, ex IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A person's month under section 14`
`pe` k x ex MEANS `mo` 2026 3 k x ex `no old-age pension` FALSE `no flags`

GIVEN k IS A `A kind of insured person under section 14`, x IS A NUMBER, e IS A `The facts that decide the exemptions of section 14(g) and (g1)`
GIVETH A `A person's month under section 14`
`pf` k x e MEANS `mo` 2026 3 k x 0 `no old-age pension` FALSE e

GIVEN k IS A `A kind of insured person under section 14`, x IS A NUMBER
      pc IS A `What old-age pension an insured person is paid`, sp IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A person's month under section 14`
`pp` k x pc sp MEANS `mo` 2026 3 k x 0 pc sp `no flags`

`supplement` MEANS `an old-age pension with an income supplement, or an additional disability benefit (section 14(e)(1))`
`plain pension` MEANS `an old-age pension without an income supplement, or a person whom section 14(e)(3) adds to (e)(2)`

`my readings` MEANS
    `The readings section 14 is applied under` WITH
        `income ceiling` IS `the maximum income of Schedule K item 1 caps the income`
        `minimum income` IS `the income is what the employee is paid`
        `reduced rate for a benefit` IS `the reduced rate applies up to the reduced amount`
        `old-age pensioner with income` IS `section 14(e) displaces section 14(b) to (d): only the fixed amount is payable`
        `computed amount of nothing` IS `decline where the readings differ`
        `benefit and income together` IS `one reduced amount across the income and the benefit together`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The figures section 14 reads for a year`
`figures` y r MEANS
    `The figures section 14 reads for a year` WITH
        `year` IS y
        `the reduced amount` IS r
        `the maximum monthly income` IS 50_695
        `the minimum amount` IS 0
        `the old-age pension amount` IS 0
        `the old-age pension amount raised for a spouse` IS 0

GIVEN q IS A `A person's month under section 14`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`h` q MEANS `the health insurance contribution for` q `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `my readings`

GIVEN k IS A `A benefit of section 14(d)(2)`, x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A benefit paid in a month`
`benefit` k x MEANS
    `A benefit paid in a month` WITH
        `year` IS 2026
        `month` IS 3
        `kind` IS k
        `amount` IS x

GIVEN k IS A `A benefit of section 14(d)(2)`, x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`b` k x MEANS
    `the contribution on a benefit, for` (`benefit` k x) `when the income in the month on which section 14(b) or (c) is also payable is` 0 `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `my readings`

